#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# register_exception_type

#% text
# `register_exception_type(type, parent)` declares `type` as an exception type that is a kind of `parent`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `register_exception_type(type)` declares a type with no parent; the parent may be a list of types.

#% item
# The value is an association of the type and its parents. The types and parents are kept for the session; `exception_types()` lists the types.

#% item
# A thrown exception is caught by `catch_exception` for its own type and for every type it is a kind of.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
register_exception_type(arg_error)
register_exception_type(arg_type_error, arg_error)
#% output
#= assoc(exception_type -> arg_type_error, parent_exception_types -> [arg_error])

#% cell
exception_types()
#% output
#= [arg_error, arg_type_error]

#% section
